{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>It is too much for you, for all the congregation, etc., and why, etc.</b> — meaning: you have taken for yourselves a great rulership beyond what is fitting. And if you ask, what is this great rulership? — that the entire congregation are all holy, and moreover HaShem is among them, something no nation in the world has attained, yet you are rulers over them. Further, they alluded in this statement to say that the Shekhinah dwelt for the glory of Israel, not for the glory of Aaron — and this is the statement <b>among them is HaShem.</b>" "And their saying <b>and why,</b> etc. — meaning: why do you add recognition of exaltedness for yourselves over them? The intention in this is that they are saying that any Israelite who draws near to the barrier within which Aaron stands is liable to death — such a one would elevate the princely office above the congregation of HaShem. And it is not fitting to degrade so greatly a holy congregation, those who draw near to El Elyon, by disqualifying them from drawing near to serve HaShem their Elohim."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:53.620547202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}